{"name":"Mon Cher Ami","hex":"#c45971","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mongolian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The former currency of Japan until 1870, before the yen.","The former currency of the Ryukyu Kingdom until its annexation by Japan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mon"},{"term":"cher","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of 'cher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cher"},{"term":"ami","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Amis."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of amigurumi."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ami"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cher Ami","blocks":[{"text":"Cher Ami was a male homing pigeon known for his military service during World War I, especially the Meuse-Argonne offensive in October 1918. According to popular legend, he delivered a message alerting American forces to the location of the Lost Battalion, despite sustaining injuries such as being shot in the breast, losing his right leg and being blinded in his left eye."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/Cher_Ami_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cher_Ami","wikidata":"Q391632"},{"title":"Cher","blocks":[{"text":"Cher is an American singer and actress. Dubbed the \"Goddess of Pop\", she is known for her androgynous, contralto voice, bold fashion, elaborate stagecraft and multifaceted career. Her screen roles often reflect her public image as a strong-willed, outspoken woman. An influential figure in popular culture, Cher has sustained a career spanning more than six decades through continual reinvention."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cher_in_2019_cropped.jpg/330px-Cher_in_2019_cropped.jpg?